// REQUIRES: gdb, lldb, host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %gopp build %S/Inputs/thunk.gopp -o %t
// RUN: timeout 30 gdb -batch -nx -q -x %S/Inputs/thunk.gdb %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GDB
// RUN: timeout 30 lldb --no-lldbinit -b -s %S/Inputs/thunk.lldb %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LLDB
// P04.12 (review R5), at `opt 0`: GIR inlines Rect.Area into the interface
// thunk `s.Area()` calls. The thunk has no source position, so its own
// locals are no variables; the copy of the method keeps its receiver and its
// local, which are the method's (decided by the method, not by the function
// it was inlined into). Both sides: in the inlined frame r and a print their
// values; in the thunk's own frame, at the method's declaration line (review
// R8), there is nothing to show.
//
// GDB: #0 {{.*}}main.Rect.Area (r=...) at {{.*}}thunk.gopp:16
// GDB-NEXT: #1 {{.*}}interface thunk for main.Rect.Area () at {{.*}}thunk.gopp:15
// GDB-NEXT: $1 = {w = 3, h = 3}
// GDB-NEXT: return a
// GDB-NEXT: $2 = 9
// GDB-NEXT: a = 9
// GDB-NEXT: #1 {{.*}}interface thunk for main.Rect.Area () at {{.*}}thunk.gopp:15
// GDB-NEXT: func (r Rect) Area() int {
// GDB-NEXT: No arguments.
// GDB-NEXT: No locals.
//
// LLDB: frame #0: {{.*}}`main.Rect.Area(r=(w = 3, h = 3)) at thunk.gopp:16:{{[0-9]+}} [inlined]
// LLDB: (main.Rect) r = (w = 3, h = 3)
// LLDB: (long) a = 9
// LLDB: frame #1: {{.*}}`interface thunk for main.Rect.Area
// LLDB: (lldb) frame variable
// LLDB-NOT: =
